/p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="155" name="Google Shape;155;p16"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1" type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="819150" y="1990725"/><a:ext cx="7505700" cy="2448000"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchorCtr="0" anchor="t" bIns="91425" lIns="91425" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="91425" wrap="square" tIns="91425"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="457200" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>Most of you people might think that there are 3 states of matter: Solid, liquid and gases. However this is incorrect. There are actually 5 states of matter: Solid,Liquids, Gas, Plasma, and Bose-Einstein. Now to describe them. Solids is a state if matter that is the heaviest. Particles move really slowly, and they have the most mass and volume out of every state. Almost everything you see is a solid. Your desks, pencils, tests, etc are all solids. </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="1600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="1600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>	Liquids on the other hand are a little bit more complex than solids. There particles are close together but they can move freely. Liquids also can be made into any object (sorta) like solids. You can for example have a cup shapes like a square and when you pour water in it the liquid takes the shape of the cup making it a square. </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="156" name="Google Shape;156;p16"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="6175275" y="215063"/><a:ext cx="2800350" cy="1628775"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="157" name="Google Shape;157;p16"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId4"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="4076597" y="215075"/><a:ext cx="2098675" cy="1378900"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr><mc:AlternateContent><mc:Choice Requires="p14"><p:transition spd="slow" p14:dur="2600"><p14:flip dir="l"/></p:transition></mc:Choice><mc:Fallback><p:transition spd="slow"><p:fade/></p:transition></mc:Fallback></mc:AlternateContent></p:sld>